name: Total attempts and retained observations stay distinct from completed-pass recurrence
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/retained_attempts.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: campaign batch-test
require-live-snap: 25 BATCH batch-test | total-attempts
expect: 2 total attempts
expect: pass 1/3
nav-mode:
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Current attempt counter: 1 | selected-attempts
expect: 2 total attempts
expect: Total attempts do not reset on resume
resize: 160x48
live-snap: detail-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: detail-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: detail-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: detail-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: detail-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: detail-paged-40x12
ask: Are total attempts, the current counter and recorded run identity distinguishable and reachable at all six sizes without suggesting that resume refunds consumption?
resize: 120x36
keys: q
require-live-snap: 20 2 total attempts | returned-jobs
keys: o
require-live-snap: 20 BATCH OCCURRENCE | opened-observations
expect: batch clear restores workspace history
keys: NPage
require-live-snap: 20 Retained outside completed passes | retained-observation
expect: seen 0 / completed 3
expect: run-trial-1-a1
ask: Does a retained observation show zero completed-pass recurrence with its exact canceled source, without implying a false positive or a fix?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/retained_attempts.py @TMP_TARGET @ART legacy
keys: PPage r
require-live-snap: 20 current attempt | legacy-attempts
expect: Lifetime totals unavailable
expect-not: 2 total attempts
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Lifetime attempt total unavailable | legacy-detail
expect: Current attempt counter: 1
ask: Does legacy history disclose the unavailable lifetime total while preserving its current counter and recorded evidence?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/retained_attempts.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restore
keys: q r
require-live-snap: 20 2 total attempts | restored-totals
keys: Escape
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 20 FINDINGS | review-readers
nav-mode:
keys: B
require-live-snap: 20 REVIEW BACKLOG | backlog-active
expect: backlog off
keys: t
require-live-snap: 20 owned-fixture | backlog-tool-filter
expect: Viewing Review
ask: Does t filter by the producing tool in backlog mode while the visible T binding retains trace access, without changing a finding decision?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: campaign batch-test
require-live-snap: 25 2 total attempts | recovered-totals
nav-mode:
keys: o
require-live-snap: 20 BATCH OCCURRENCE | recovered-observations
keys: NPage
require-live-snap: 20 Retained outside completed passes | recovered-recurrence
expect: seen 0 / completed 3
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/retained_attempts.py @TMP_TARGET @ART verify
ask: Does no-color restart retain attempt consumption and honest recurrence without new discovery, provider calls or finding decisions?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
